# TUI-DESIGN-3 §4.4 F21 live: `/undo` while a run is live is an availability error (`runs when the run is idle`) and clears the draft — the
# next line is not `/undo/pause`; one Ctrl-C then aborts the live run (the draft is gone); /exit leaves 0
expect \x1b\[\?25l
expect Say hi
sleep 0.3
send make the tests pass
sleep 0.2
send \r
expect step \d+/\d+
expect Type to steer
send /undo
sleep 0.2
send \r
expect idle|live run|not available
sleep 0.3
# F21: the availability error cleared the draft, so ONE Ctrl-C aborts the live run (a kept draft would swallow it — that is the
# assertion); two in a row would be the double-Ctrl-C exit instead of the abort
send \x03
expect finished [·-] human_abort
expect Follow-up, question
send /exit
sleep 0.2
send \r
eof
